    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "straight_channels_parallel_to_(0k0)_surface → diffusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "pore_channels_parallel_to_large_top_surface → diffusion"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] balance intracrystalline diffusion and surface permeation when tuning framework structure for kinetic C3H6/C3H8 separation → identified as an essential starting point for effective kinetic adsorptive separation, especially for gases with highly similar kinetic size"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] use a pore window size comparable to the molecular cross-sections of C3H6 and C3H8, as in Zn-ATA with a 4.1 × 3.8 Å2 window → enables kinetic discrimination, with C3H6 adsorbing dramatically faster than C3H8 in Milli-Zn-ATA"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "C3H6 adsorption in Milli-Zn-ATA vs C3H8 adsorption in Milli-Zn-ATA: winner=subject_a on adsorption_rate"
    }
  ],
